{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676096",
      "title": "A Brief Look at the Remix Config File",
      "lectureOrder": 110,
      "videoOrder": 103,
      "sourceHash": "cf9374de7deed67e48075e90d20540b5bdcc622822130ef83b24661e932209d4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "Now before we'll dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 5.58,
          "en": "into a concrete deployment example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.58,
          "end": 8.37,
          "en": "there's one last thing we should take a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.37,
          "end": 10.41,
          "en": "and that's the Remix config file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.41,
          "end": 13.41,
          "en": "the configuration we can apply to Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.41,
          "end": 15.99,
          "en": "Now arguably the best place to dive deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.99,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "on that is the official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 20.1,
          "en": "because most of these conflict settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.1,
          "end": 22.53,
          "en": "are only needed in niche scenarios.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.53,
          "end": 25.29,
          "en": "So that's the best place to learn about all of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 27.42,
          "en": "But there are three settings here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.42,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "which I do wanna highlight.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 32.94,
          "en": "The first setting is this ignore route files setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 35.1,
          "en": "which is actually enabled by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.1,
          "end": 37.59,
          "en": "and which by default ignores all files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.59,
          "end": 41.01,
          "en": "in the route folder that start with a dot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.01,
          "end": 44.63,
          "en": "What this setting does is, it simply defines which files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.63,
          "end": 48.18,
          "en": "in the route folder will not be treated as routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 50.28,
          "en": "because by default all files in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.28,
          "end": 51.84,
          "en": "will be treated as routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.84,
          "end": 53.58,
          "en": "But this setting, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.58,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "ensures that files starting with a dot will be ignored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 59.94,
          "en": "So invisible files, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.94,
          "end": 63.21,
          "en": "We could also add a pattern like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.21,
          "end": 66.3,
          "en": "to ignore any CSS files in that folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.3,
          "end": 70.65,
          "en": "so that if we planned to have a specific CSS files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.65,
          "end": 72.72,
          "en": "next to our component files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 77.22,
          "en": "we could do that without adding any new routes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.22,
          "end": 81.66,
          "en": "If we add the appropriate setting here in Remix config JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.66,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "we will ignore those CSS files just fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 86.61,
          "en": "And you can add as many settings here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 86.61,
          "end": 89.88,
          "en": "as many to be ignored files as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.88,
          "end": 93.57,
          "en": "So that's the first setting that's worth a closer look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.57,
          "end": 95.07,
          "en": "Another interesting setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.07,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "is the assets built directory setting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 98.97,
          "en": "which is by default not enabled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.97,
          "end": 101.19,
          "en": "but there is a default setting for this setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.19,
          "end": 102.693,
          "en": "It's just not overwritten.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 106.74000000000001,
          "en": "Now here you could override the default path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.74000000000001,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "for the build output of Remix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "and we will run a build command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 112.95,
          "en": "in the next lecture again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "to prepare the application for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 118.4,
          "en": "And what that build command will do is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.4,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "it will generate a couple of optimized JavaScript files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 125.76,
          "en": "that in the end also make up our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 125.76,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "Now, if you plan to deploy your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "such that your public files, like for example, images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "that should be accessible to everyone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 136.14,
          "en": "are not stored in a folder named public,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.14,
          "end": 138.42000000000002,
          "en": "then you should also update this path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 138.42000000000002,
          "end": 140.31,
          "en": "to ensure that this build path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 140.31,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "is in the folder that will be publicly accessible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 146.61,
          "en": "Because the output, the build output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.61,
          "end": 150.42000000000002,
          "en": "must be in such a publicly accessible folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 150.42000000000002,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "So therefore, by default you don't need to change this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 155.55,
          "en": "but if you plan on using some other folder than public",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 159.45,
          "en": "you would need to update this build output path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.45,
          "end": 161.64,
          "en": "setting here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 161.64,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "And the last setting which I wanna highlight",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "is this server dependencies to bundle setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 171.3,
          "en": "It's not commented out here in this default setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.3,
          "end": 173.55,
          "en": "which I have here, but we could nonetheless",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.55,
          "end": 177.9,
          "en": "add it here, this server dependencies to bundle setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 177.9,
          "end": 179.82,
          "en": "And what this setting does is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 183.99,
          "en": "it allows you to specify an array of identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 183.99,
          "end": 186.93,
          "en": "that identify third party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 186.93,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "you might have in your package dot JSON file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 195.15,
          "en": "which do not support common JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.15,
          "end": 198.51,
          "en": "Now, common JS is basically an approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 198.51,
          "end": 202.11,
          "en": "for importing JavaScript files into each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.11,
          "end": 205.82999999999998,
          "en": "and an approach for combining JavaScript files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 205.82999999999998,
          "end": 209.01,
          "en": "The alternative is ES modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 209.01,
          "end": 211.95,
          "en": "Now the import export syntax we used in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 211.95,
          "end": 215.7,
          "en": "with the import statement is actually ES modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.7,
          "end": 219.12,
          "en": "though not really, we're just using this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 219.12,
          "end": 222.27,
          "en": "during development, but behind the scenes it is translated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 222.27,
          "end": 225.99,
          "en": "to a different syntax, to the common JS syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 225.99,
          "end": 227.61,
          "en": "You don't need to know the details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 227.61,
          "end": 229.5,
          "en": "but it is important to understand that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 229.5,
          "end": 233.4,
          "en": "there are these two different systems for combining files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 233.4,
          "end": 235.77,
          "en": "And under the hood, at least at the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 235.77,
          "end": 238.623,
          "en": "I'm recording this, Remix uses common JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.64,
          "end": 242.1,
          "en": "There are some third party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.1,
          "end": 244.47,
          "en": "which don't support this system though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 244.47,
          "end": 246.51,
          "en": "and which therefore could cause errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 246.51,
          "end": 248.34,
          "en": "We don't have them here in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 248.34,
          "end": 250.62,
          "en": "but such packages exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 250.62,
          "end": 253.23,
          "en": "And if you do get such errors where you basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 253.23,
          "end": 256.59,
          "en": "get complaints about a package being ESM only,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 256.59,
          "end": 259.17,
          "en": "then you can simply add that package name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 259.17,
          "end": 261.12,
          "en": "to server dependencies to bundle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 261.12,
          "end": 264.09,
          "en": "so that Remix will treat it differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 264.09,
          "end": 266.43,
          "en": "behind the scenes you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 266.43,
          "end": 269.52,
          "en": "So it's also setting you probably don't need all the time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 269.52,
          "end": 271.77,
          "en": "but for certain packages you might need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 271.77,
          "end": 274.56,
          "en": "And since I don't want you to encounter this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 274.56,
          "end": 278.49,
          "en": "ESM package error without knowing what you can do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 278.49,
          "end": 280.83299999999997,
          "en": "I wanted to show this setting as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 281.94,
          "end": 284.01,
          "en": "But that's it for this configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 284.01,
          "end": 286.653,
          "en": "Now let's take a look at an example deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
